course: dictionary
lesson: 11582
title: The antagonist
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The antagonist is the main enemy or opponent of the hero in a story, play or film. The hero is called the protagonist, so the two are opposites. «The brave knight Sam wanted to save the village, but the wicked Baron Grim wanted to steal its gold.» Baron Grim is the antagonist.
explain: The antagonist does not always have to be a monster. It can be a rival, a bully or anyone who gets in the hero's way. «Maya wanted to win the science prize, but her rival Tom kept hiding her experiment notes.» Tom is the antagonist, because he works against Maya.
explain: The word can also describe a real person who strongly opposes someone. «Jo became the antagonist of the new rule, arguing against it at every meeting.» Jo is not a villain in a film here. She is someone who strongly opposes the rule.
explain: In science, an antagonist is a muscle or chemical that works against another. Your biceps and triceps are an antagonistic pair: when the biceps pulls, the triceps relaxes, so your elbow bends. When the triceps pulls, the biceps relaxes, so your elbow straightens.
fact: An antagonist is the main enemy or opponent of the hero.
fact: The protagonist is the hero, and the antagonist is the opposite of the protagonist.
fact: An antagonist can be a person, a group, or even a force that gets in the way of the hero.
fact: Someone who strongly opposes another person can also be called an antagonist.
fact: In biology, muscles often work in antagonistic pairs, such as the biceps and triceps.
exercise: «The wicked Baron Grim wanted to steal the village gold, and he tried every trick to stop the brave hero.» Who is the antagonist? | The brave hero | *Baron Grim | The village | The gold
exercise: What is the opposite of the protagonist in a story? | Setting | Chapter | *Antagonist | Narrator
exercise: Your biceps bends your elbow and your triceps straightens it. What do we call a muscle that works against another muscle? | Protagonist | Narrator | *Antagonist | Synonym
test: «Maya wanted to win the race, but her rival Tom kept tripping her up.» Who is the antagonist in this sentence? | Maya | The race | Nobody, because there is no villain | *Tom
test: In science, what is an antagonist? | A friend who always helps | A type of bird | The main hero of a film | *A muscle or chemical that works against another
exam: Which character is the antagonist? «Lily, the brave knight, rode out to save the king from the wicked sorcerer.» | *The wicked sorcerer | The castle | Lily | The king
